>
  <p>
    When engineering location-based applications—such as delivery dispatch systems, dating apps, transit trackers, or geofencing utilities—developers and QA testers need to simulate coordinates across different continents without physically travelling there.
  </p>
  <p>
    Modern operating systems include dedicated <strong>Mock Location APIs</strong> designed specifically for testing. In this guide, we detail how to emulate GPS coordinates on desktop browsers, Android, and iOS, how mock location flags work under the hood, and how to verify mock fixes with our <a href="/tools/gps-coordinates/">GPS Coordinates Finder</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="tool-callout">
    <div class="tool-callout-content">
      <span class="tool-callout-badge">🧪 Live Coordinate Verification</span>
      <h3 class="tool-callout-title">Verify Your Emulated GPS Coordinates</h3>
